# Config-based hooks (Git 2.54+) for this repository only.
#
# Pulled in from .gitconfig via `includeIf hasconfig:remote.*.url:`, so these
# fire only in the dotfiles clone -- not in every repo on the machine. The
# match is on the remote URL rather than `gitdir:` on purpose: ~/git/dotfiles
# is a symlink to ~/git/github.com/delphinus/dotfiles, and `gitdir:` compares
# against the resolved path, so the path everyone actually types would never
# match (measured 2026-09-08).
#
# Because both this file and the scripts it points at are tracked, a plain
# `git pull` is enough to update them on another machine. Nothing has to be
# written into .git/hooks, which git never tracks.
#
# Requires Git 2.54.0 or newer. On older Git these keys are unknown config and
# are ignored *silently*, which is why ansible still installs shims into
# .git/hooks; those shims stand down as soon as `git hook list` reports the
# hooks below. See ansible/templates/git_hooks_*.j2.

[hook "gitleaks-staged"]
	event = pre-commit
	command = ~/git/dotfiles/bin/gitleaks-pre-commit

[hook "gitleaks-message"]
	event = commit-msg
	command = ~/git/dotfiles/bin/gitleaks-commit-msg

